    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d112">

                <pb facs="0194" n="186" sameAs="frus:frus1941v04/pg186"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">711.94/2086</note>
                <head>
                    <hi rendition="#italic">The Japanese Ambassador</hi> (<hi rendition="#italic"
                        >Nomura</hi>) <hi rendition="#italic">to the Secretary of State </hi><anchor
                        n="43" xml:id="d112-f1"/>
                </head>
                <dateline>
                    <date ana="#date_undated-inferred-from-document-head" calendar="gregorian"
                        type="conversation-or-meeting-date" when="1941-05-12">undated</date>
                </dateline>
                <p rendition="#center">
                    <hi rendition="#small-caps">Project</hi>
                </p>
                <p>I anticipate that the United States Government will propose explanations to the
                    Understanding corresponding to the explanations submitted by me. The
                    explanations submitted by me regarding the Understanding were official and in
                    accordance with the instructions received from our Government. When both
                    explanations are agreed upon by mutual accord, they should be deemed a mutually
                    official supplement to the Understanding.</p>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
    <standOff>
        <listAnnotation>
            <note corresp="#d112-f1" n="43" type="source" xml:id="d112-f1-content">
                <p>Notation on file copy: “About May 12, 1941. See Japanese ‘explanations’ received
                    on May 12, 1941 and memorandum of conversation May 12, 1941.” For these
                    documents, see <ref target="frus1931-41v02#pg_423">
                        <hi rendition="#italic">Foreign Relations</hi>, Japan, 1931–1941, vol. <hi
                            rendition="#small-caps">ii</hi>, pp. 423</ref> and <ref
                        target="frus1931-41v02#pg_418">418</ref>, respectively. For draft proposal
                    of May 12, see <ref target="frus1931-41v02#pg_420">
                        <hi rendition="#italic">ibid.</hi>, p. 420</ref>.</p>
            </note>
        </listAnnotation>
    </standOff>
